{"agent":"bugs-block-abandoned","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The intent states the MCP description was left unchanged (\"to keep the byte budget\"), so it still advertises only that a **DONE** item is refused unless `reopen`. After this diff the same exit‑3 refusal now also fires for **ABANDONED** items, so the machine‑facing contract the MCP server hands to agents is now false. Concretely: an agent that reads only the tool schema, with `T1` in state `abandoned`, calls `ddflow_block` with `{\"id\":\"T1\",\"reason\":\"x\"}` (no `reopen`); the advertised description implies the call succeeds, but the server returns `_meta.exit == 3` and performs no state change (this is exactly what the new `test_block_abandoned_over_mcp_needs_reopen` asserts). The agent has no prior indication that `--reopen`/`reopen=true` is required for this state, so the schema it was given does not match the behavior it gets. This is a behavior/contract defect on a user‑visible surface rather than a cosmetic doc issue: the tool description is the interface agents route on, and it now under-specifies the refusal condition the code enforces.","digest":"92473f1ec35f756f","location":"ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py (the `ddflow_block` tool description)","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py (the `ddflow_block` tool description)"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":4626,"diff_sha":"908f4eaed7f95e6d8f72e015549a14b77733ebf5202d5e273ae86f25d20cfdc5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-fix-block-abandoned","elapsed_s":107.7,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py (the `ddflow_block` tool description)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","